  "chiral_algebra": "\\big(SU(2)_{5}\\times U(1)_2\\big)/U(1)_{7}",
  "irreducible": true,
  "Z_tex": "Z = \\sum_{(l,m,s)/\\sim} |\\chi^l_{m,s}|^2",
  "character_tex": "Branching functions $\\chi^{SU(2)_k}_l(\\tau,z)\\,\\Theta_{s,2}(\\tau,z) = \\sum_{m\\in\\mathbb{Z}_{2(k+2)}} \\chi^l_{m,s}(\\tau)\\,\\Theta_{m,k+2}(\\tau,z)$, $\\Theta_{m,K}(\\tau,z) = \\sum_{n\\in\\mathbb{Z}+m/2K} q^{Kn^2}z^{Kn}$ (Sugawara, arXiv:2004.05742, eq. (A.16) at zero $U(1)$ fugacity), computed from the Weyl-Kac character $\\chi_l$ as $\\chi^l_{m,s} = q^{-u^2/(k+2)}\\,[z^u]\\big(\\chi_l\\,\\Theta_{s,2}\\big)$ for any $u \\in \\frac m2 + (k+2)\\mathbb{Z}$. Labels: $l+m+s$ even, $(l,m,s)\\sim(k-l,\\,m+k+2,\\,s+2)$; each orbit is labelled by its representative with $s\\in\\{0,1\\}$ ($s=0$ NS, $s=1$ R) and $-(k+2)<m\\le k+2$. For $|m-s|\\le l$ the weight is $h = \\frac{l(l+2)-m^2}{4(k+2)} + \\frac{s}{8}$. The NS and R characters of the $\\mathcal{N}=2$ algebra are $\\chi^l_{m,0}+\\chi^l_{m,2}$ and $\\chi^l_{m,1}+\\chi^l_{m,3}$.",
  "description": "Bosonic diagonal coset theory at $k=5$: one term $|\\chi^l_{m,s}|^2$ for each of the 84 field-identification orbits, so the NS$\\otimes$NS and R$\\otimes$R sectors appear with $s_L = s_R$ and there is no NS$\\otimes$R sector. The supercurrents $G^\\pm$ appear only paired with antiholomorphic fermionic states; the lowest are the four states $G^a\\bar G^b$ at $(h,\\bar h) = (\\frac32,\\frac32)$, in the block of the orbit of $(0,0,2)$, labelled $\\chi^{5}_{7,0}$. This is the diagonal invariant $Z = \\sum_{(a,c)\\in Q_k}|\\chi_{a,c}|^2$ of Cordova-Rizi (arXiv:2312.17308, eq. (2.31)) and Gray (arXiv:0812.1318, eq. (4) with $M$ the identity), the bosonization of the fermionic $\\mathcal{N}=2$ minimal model (Chen-Duan-Jia-Lee, arXiv:2511.22129, supplement A).",
  "generator": "scripts/spectra/gen_n2.py",
